 "B3.2"]}, "discriminator_hints": "[Knowledge Layer: coverage=56%, source=both]\n\nInfectious Gastroenteritis vs Irritable Bowel Syndrome with Constipation (IBS-C):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the gastrointestinal tract, ascites, atopic dermatitis, bloody diarrhea, body aches\n  Favours second: abdominal bloating, abnormal auditory evoked potentials, abnormal cerebellum morphology, abnormal cerebral white matter morphology, abnormal facial shape\n\nInfectious Gastroenteritis vs Chronic Intestinal Pseudo-Obstruction:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the gastrointestinal tract, atopic dermatitis, bloody diarrhea, body aches, chills\n  Favours second: abdominal distention, abnormal rectum morphology, abnormality of metabolism/homeostasis, abnormality of the hepatic vasculature, abnormality of the liver\n\nInfectious Gastroenteritis vs Acute Mesenteric Ischemia:\n  Favours first:  abdominal pain, abnormality of the gastrointestinal tract, ascites, atopic dermatitis, bloody diarrhea\n  Favours second: abnormal bleeding, abnormal cardiac ventricular function, abnormal cornea morphology, abnormal cutaneous elastic fiber morphology, abnormal facial shape\n\nInfectious Gastroenteritis vs Chronic Mesenteric Ischemia (Atherosclerotic):\n  Favours first:  abdominal pain, abnormality of the gastrointestinal tract, ascites, atopic dermatitis, bloody diarrhea\n  Favours second: cold extremities, gangrene, hair loss on legs, intermittent claudication, ischemic rest pain\n\nIrritable Bowel Syndrome with Constipation (IBS-C) vs Chronic Intestinal Pseudo-Obstruction:\n  Favours first:  abdominal bloating, abnormal auditory evoked potentials, abnormal cerebellum morphology, abnormal cerebral white matter morphology, abnormal facial shape\n  Favours second: abdominal distention, abnormality of metabolism/homeostasis, abnormality of the hepatic vasculature, abnormality of the liver, anasarca\n\nIrritable Bowel Syndrome with Constipation (IBS-C) vs Acute Mesenteric Ischemia:\n  Favours first:  abdominal bloating, abdominal pain, abnormal auditory evoked potentials, abnormal cerebellum morphology, abnormal cerebral white matter morphology\n  Favours second: abnormal bleeding, abnormal cardiac ventricular function, abnormal cornea morphology, abnormal cutaneous elastic fiber morphology, abnormal isoelectric focusing of serum transferrin\n\nIrritable Bowel Syndrome with Constipation (IBS-C) vs Chronic Mesenteric Ischemia (Atherosclerotic):\n  Favours first:  abdominal bloating, abdominal pain, abnormal auditory evoked potentials, abnormal cerebellum morphology, abnormal cerebral white matter morphology\n  Favours second: cold extremities, gangrene, hair loss on legs, intermittent claudication, ischemic rest pain\n\nChronic Intestinal Pseudo-Obstruction vs Acute Mesenteric Ischemia:\n  Favours first:  abdominal distention, abdominal pain, abnormal rectum morphology, abnormality of metabolism/homeostasis, abnormality of the hepatic vasculature\n  Favours second: abnormal bleeding, abnormal cardiac ventricular function, abnormal cornea morphology, abnormal cutaneous elastic fiber morphology, abnormal facial shape\n\nChronic Intestinal Pseudo-Obstruction vs Chronic Mesenteric Ischemia (Atherosclerotic):\n  Favours first:  abdominal distention, abdominal pain, abnormal rectum morphology, abnormality of metabolism/homeostasis, abnormality of the hepatic vasculature\n  Favours second: cold extremities, gangrene, hair loss on legs, intermittent claudication, ischemic rest pain\n\nAcute Mesenteric Ischemia vs Chronic Mesenteric Ischemia (Atherosclerotic):\n  Favours first:  abnormal bleeding, abnormal cardiac ventricular function, abnormal cornea morphology, abnormal cutaneous elastic fiber morphology, abnormal facial shape\n  Favours second: cold extremities, hair loss on legs, intermittent claudication, ischemic rest pain, numbness in legs or feet\n\nRelated to Infectious Gastroenteritis: campylobacteriosis, colitis (disease), enteritis\n\nRelated to I